# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development (Postgres on your machine)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env`. Prisma reads this file for CLI commands (migrate, studio).
#
# For local Postgres, set DIRECT_URL to the same value as DATABASE_URL.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/in_the_kitchen?schema=public"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/in_the_kitchen?schema=public"

# Optional: override demo user password when running `pnpm db:seed`
# DEMO_USER_PASSWORD="demo1234"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (hosted Postgres for production / Vercel)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Create a project: https://supabase.com/dashboard → New project (save the DB password).
# 2. Open Connect: https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/_/sql (use top bar "Connect" / Project Settings → Database).
# 3. Serverless (Vercel): use Transaction pooler for DATABASE_URL and Session pooler for DIRECT_URL.
#    - Transaction (port 6543): append `?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1` (required for Prisma + pooler).
#    - Session (port 5432): use for migrations (Prisma uses DIRECT_URL for migrate deploy).
#    Example shape (replace host, user, password, project ref, region):
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
#
# If you use a dedicated `prisma` role, replace `postgres` in the user part with `prisma` and run
# scripts/sql/supabase-prisma-role.sql first (set a strong password in SQL and in your URIs).
#
# Prisma + Supabase guide: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/prisma
# Troubleshooting: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/prisma/prisma-troubleshooting
#
# Optional: if you only use Prisma server-side and not the Supabase Data API (PostgREST) for these tables,
# you can turn off the Data API in Supabase → Settings → API (see Supabase Prisma guide).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables, add BOTH:
#   DATABASE_URL  (transaction pooler URI + ?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1)
#   DIRECT_URL    (session pooler URI, port 5432)
# Then redeploy. On Vercel (`VERCEL=1`) the build runs `prisma migrate deploy` then `next build`
# (see scripts/build.mjs). Locally, `pnpm build` runs `next build` only.
#
# One-time against the Supabase DB (from your machine, same URLs as Vercel):
#   pnpm db:migrate
#   pnpm db:seed
#
# Verify production: https://<your-domain>/api/health — expect ok: true, dbReachable: true.
